# PART 1 — ORGANISATION AND ACCOUNT STRUCTURE

DriveMitra is an organisation-based fleet management platform.

Each subscribing customer represents a fleet organisation.

### Organisation hierarchy

Platform Administrator
    |
    |-- Fleet Organisation A
    |      |
    |      |-- Fleet Owner
    |      |-- Staff Members
    |      |-- Drivers
    |      |-- Vehicles
    |      |-- Assignments
    |      |-- Trips
    |      |-- Maintenance
    |      |-- Finance
    |      |-- Contracts
    |
    |-- Fleet Organisation B
           |
           |-- Fleet Owner
           |-- Staff Members
           |-- Drivers
           |-- Vehicles
           |-- Assignments
           |-- Trips
           |-- Maintenance
           |-- Finance
           |-- Contracts

Every organisation must have isolated records.

Organisation A must never be able to access Organisation B's private information.

Use a consistent organisation identifier across all tenant-owned records.

Do not rely only on frontend organisation filters. Enforce tenant isolation in backend queries and authorisation.

## 1.1 Account types

Implement these four account types:

1. PLATFORM_ADMIN
2. FLEET_OWNER
3. FLEET_STAFF
4. FLEET_DRIVER

Each account must have:
- Unique internal user ID.
- Organisation ID, where applicable.
- Role.
- Account status.
- Authentication credentials.
- Creation date.
- Last login.
- Activity history.

A Driver Record and a Driver Login Account are separate concepts.

A person may exist as a driver record without having mobile application credentials.

Only create or activate a login account when the authorised account creation or invitation workflow is completed.

