# PART 2 — FLEET OWNER LOGIC

## 2.1 Owner registration

The Fleet Owner is the primary customer and administrator of their fleet organisation.

The owner must be able to register a new organisation.

### Registration page

Required fields:

- Owner Full Name.
- Mobile Number.
- Email Address.
- Password.
- Confirm Password.
- Fleet/Organisation Name.
- Business Type.
- Fleet Location.
- Terms and Conditions Acceptance.

Business Type examples:
- Transport.
- Logistics.
- Passenger Transport.
- Goods Transportation.
- School/Staff Transportation.
- Construction Fleet.
- Other.

Allow additional organisation details to be completed after registration.

### Registration workflow

Step 1:
Owner enters personal and organisation details.

Step 2:
Validate email and mobile according to the supported verification process.

Step 3:
Create the owner account and organisation in a pending state.

Step 4:
Direct the owner to the onboarding process.

Step 5:
Collect required organisation details.

Step 6:
Require the owner to add at least one staff member.

Step 7:
Allow the owner to add drivers. This is optional.

Step 8:
Present the subscription selection page.

Step 9:
Owner selects Monthly or Annual.

Step 10:
Owner completes payment.

Step 11:
Payment must be verified.

Step 12:
Activate the subscription and organisation access.

Important:
Do not grant paid operational access merely because the user registered or selected a subscription plan.

If the owner has not completed payment verification, show the appropriate pending-payment or activation state.

## 2.2 Mandatory staff requirement

A Fleet Owner must add at least one staff member during organisation onboarding.

Implement this as an onboarding requirement, not an arbitrary vehicle or employee subscription limit.

Rules:
- At least one staff record must be created.
- The owner can invite the staff member.
- The invitation can remain pending.
- The onboarding system must distinguish between a created staff record and an activated staff login.
- The owner can continue managing onboarding according to the configured workflow.
- Do not falsely report that the staff member has accepted an invitation.

If the staff member has not accepted the invitation, display:

Staff Invitation Pending.

Do not count the owner as the required staff member.

## 2.3 Driver requirement

Drivers are optional during initial onboarding.

The owner can:
- Add drivers during onboarding.
- Add drivers later.
- Invite drivers to the mobile application.
- Maintain driver records without login access.
- Activate or deactivate driver accounts.
- Assign and reassign vehicles.
- Upload and maintain driver documents.

There must not be an artificial requirement to add a driver before activating a fleet.

## 2.4 Owner permissions

The Fleet Owner has full authority over their organisation's operational and business modules.

The owner can:

### Organisation management
- Edit organisation profile.
- Manage fleet information.
- Manage subscription.
- Manage billing information.
- Manage organisation settings.

### Staff management
- Add staff.
- Invite staff.
- Edit staff.
- Configure permissions.
- Suspend staff.
- Reactivate staff.
- Review staff activity.

### Driver management
- Add drivers.
- Edit drivers.
- Upload documents.
- Manage licences.
- Assign vehicles.
- Manage driver accounts.
- Review driver activity.

### Fleet management
- Add and edit vehicles.
- Manage vehicle assignments.
- Manage trips.
- Manage inspections.
- Manage issues.
- Manage maintenance.
- Manage work orders.
- Manage fuel and expenses.
- Manage inventory.
- Manage tyre records.
- Manage reminders.

### Financial management
- Manage vehicle finance.
- Manage EMI schedules.
- Record payments.
- Review expenses.
- Manage contract payments.
- Manage deposits.
- Review reports.

### Other management
- Manage contacts.
- Manage vendors.
- Manage documents.
- Manage warranties.
- Manage custom records.
- Manage approval workflows.
- Manage notifications.

### Owner restriction

Integrations are exclusively controlled by the Platform Administrator.

The Fleet Owner must not access platform-level integration credentials, server settings or other organisations' data.

The owner must also not be able to grant permissions exceeding their own authority.

