# PART 3 — STAFF LOGIC

## 3.1 Staff account creation

The Fleet Owner creates staff accounts.

Staff cannot independently register a new fleet organisation through the staff invitation workflow.

### Add Staff page

Fields:

- Full Name.
- Mobile Number.
- Email Address.
- Employee ID.
- Designation.
- Department.
- Login Username, if supported.
- Assigned Responsibilities.
- Initial Permissions.

### Staff creation workflow

1. Owner opens Staff Directory.
2. Clicks Add Staff.
3. Enters staff information.
4. Selects role or responsibility.
5. Configures permissions.
6. Sends invitation or creates an account using the supported authentication workflow.
7. Staff receives invitation.
8. Staff completes account activation.
9. Staff can sign in.
10. Activity is recorded.

### Staff account statuses

- Draft.
- Invitation Pending.
- Active.
- Suspended.
- Deactivated.

Do not confuse staff employment status with login account status.

## 3.2 Staff permission system

The Fleet Owner must be able to customise permissions individually.

Do not implement only fixed Staff and Manager roles.

Support permission configuration at:
- Module level.
- Page level, where necessary.
- Action level.
- Sensitive-field level.

### Permission types

| Permission | Meaning |
|---|---|
| View | View permitted records |
| Add | Create records |
| Edit | Modify records |
| Delete | Delete records where safe and permitted |
| Approve | Approve permitted workflows |
| Export | Export permitted information |
| Manage | Manage module settings or configuration |

### Default staff permission matrix

Use this as the initial restricted permission profile.

