# PART 8 — PAYMENT AND SUBSCRIPTION ACTIVATION

## 8.1 Checkout page

Display:
- Organisation Name.
- Selected Plan.
- Billing Period.
- Base Amount.
- Applicable Tax.
- Total Payable.
- Payment Status.
- Payment Method.

Buttons:
- Proceed to Payment.
- Change Plan.
- Cancel Checkout.

Use a supported payment gateway only after verifying its configuration and integration requirements.

Do not simulate successful payments.

## 8.2 Payment lifecycle

Use payment states such as:

- Created.
- Pending.
- Processing.
- Successful.
- Failed.
- Cancelled.
- Refunded.
- Partially Refunded.

Maintain subscription status separately from payment status.

A successful payment record alone must not bypass the subscription activation process.

Verify payment using trusted server-side gateway confirmation or an authorised Platform Administrator verification process.

Never trust a frontend success message as proof of payment.

## 8.3 Activation

After payment verification:

1. Confirm organisation identity.
2. Confirm selected plan.
3. Confirm payment amount.
4. Confirm payment status.
5. Check for duplicate payment processing.
6. Create or activate the subscription.
7. Set billing start date.
8. Calculate the billing end date.
9. Set the next renewal date.
10. Enable authorised organisation access.
11. Record activation history.
12. Notify the Fleet Owner.

For a monthly subscription, use the appropriate monthly billing period.

For an annual subscription, use the appropriate annual billing period.

Use reliable date calculations that handle month-end and leap-year boundaries.

## 8.4 Subscription statuses

Implement:

- Pending Payment.
- Pending Verification.
- Active.
- Renewal Due.
- Past Due.
- Grace Period, if configured.
- Expired.
- Suspended.
- Cancelled.

Do not confuse subscription status with organisation status or user account status.

## 8.5 Subscription expiration

When a subscription expires:

- Stop access to paid operational functionality according to the configured policy.
- Preserve all organisation data.
- Preserve documents and historical records.
- Display an expiration notice.
- Provide renewal options.
- Do not delete the organisation.
- Do not delete vehicles, drivers, trips, expenses or contracts.
- Do not silently remove users.

Implement a clear read-only or restricted-access policy for expired organisations.

The exact grace-period duration and access policy must be explicitly configurable and visible to the owner.

Do not invent a grace period.

## 8.6 Renewal

Monthly:
- Generate the next billing period.
- Display the renewal amount.
- Record the payment.
- Extend access after successful verification.

Annual:
- Generate the annual renewal.
- Display the renewal amount.
- Record the payment.
- Extend access after successful verification.

Do not extend subscriptions based on an unverified payment attempt.

## 8.7 Cancellation

Provide a subscription cancellation workflow.

The owner should be able to:
- View current subscription.
- View billing dates.
- Request cancellation.
- Review cancellation consequences.
- Confirm cancellation.
- View cancellation status.

Preserve access according to the actual paid-through period and configured cancellation policy.

Do not automatically delete customer data after cancellation.

