# PART 10 — IMPORTANT CROSS-MODULE BUSINESS RULES

These rules must be checked across the entire application.

## 10.1 Vehicle and driver assignment

- One vehicle cannot have conflicting active assignments unless explicitly supported.
- A driver cannot have conflicting active trip assignments.
- A driver must be authorised to operate the assigned vehicle.
- Assignment history must be preserved.
- Changing a driver must not erase previous assignments.

## 10.2 Vehicle ownership and contracts

A vehicle must distinguish:
- Legal Owner.
- Operating Organisation.
- Contract Supplier.
- Operational Status.
- Maintenance Responsibility.
- Financial Responsibility.

Company-owned, fleet-contracted and individually supplied vehicles must work correctly.

## 10.3 Driver and user accounts

- Driver record and login account are separate.
- Deactivating a login must not automatically delete the driver record.
- Changing an assigned vehicle must not erase driver history.
- A driver must only access authorised records.

## 10.4 Staff permissions

- Permissions must be enforced on frontend and backend.
- Owner can customise staff access.
- Staff cannot grant themselves additional permissions.
- Staff cannot exceed owner authority.
- Revoked permissions must take effect without relying on a fresh frontend deployment.

## 10.5 Maintenance

- Issues and work orders are separate.
- Service tasks and service entries are separate.
- A completed work order can generate a linked service entry.
- Opening a work order must not create a completed service record.
- Service completion must update relevant reminders according to the configured service rules.

## 10.6 Fuel and expenses

- Fuel transactions must link to valid vehicles.
- Driver submissions must link to the submitting driver.
- Odometer values must be validated.
- Fuel approval and payment are separate.
- Expense approval and payment are separate.
- Rejected records must remain auditable.

## 10.7 Finance

- EMI schedule must remain connected to the correct finance record.
- Partial payments must be supported.
- Outstanding principal must be calculated correctly.
- A due date passing must not mark an EMI as paid.
- Payment reconciliation must be auditable.

## 10.8 Documents

- Documents must have a valid owner or related record.
- Expiry dates must generate reminders.
- Access permissions must be enforced.
- Replacing a document must preserve version history where supported.

## 10.9 Organisation isolation

Test every module for tenant isolation.

Organisation A must never access:
- Organisation B's vehicles.
- Organisation B's drivers.
- Organisation B's staff.
- Organisation B's financial information.
- Organisation B's contracts.
- Organisation B's documents.
- Organisation B's reports.

This must be enforced by backend authorisation and database query scoping.

